BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ritual – Gemini Pride Edition
DTSTART:20260530T183000
DTEND:20260530T183000
UID:438bdba031ab23b97fc9454244ff3816@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Ritual Story &amp\; Collective Art Project After being lai
 d off last year from our decade-long corporate roles as a Creative Directo
 r and a Director of Culture &amp\; Change Management\, my partner and I de
 cided to channel our energy into something we felt was missing in the city
 . We love electronic music and deeply value community\, but we often felt 
 there was a tradeoff: go to a non-queer event with incredible sound and cu
 ration\, or a queer event with subpar sound. We launched Ritual to bridge 
 that gap. A house music ritual isn&#x27\;t about escape\; it’s about a r
 eturn—to the body\, to rhythm\, and to each other. In a culture driven b
 y speed and performance\, we prioritize deep grooves and true presence. Si
 nce launching at the beginning of the year\, we&#x27\;ve held monthly\, en
 tirely free events. We hand-print and distribute intention cards to person
 ally greet every single person who enters the space\, ensuring they feel w
 elcome\, seen\, and included. We&#x27\;ve loved collaborating with local q
 ueer spaces from Understory to Old&#x27\;s Cool General Store\, and our go
 al this year is to continue to grow and diversify our community offerings.
  Our Collective Art Project for May 30: For the Gemini Pride Edition\, we 
 are inviting everyone attending to bring an old piece of clothing\, a scar
 f\, a textile\, or a piece of fabric—something once loved\, worn\, dance
 d in\, or lived in. Throughout the night\, we will collectively weave thes
 e pieces into a large community art installation inspired by the Ritual sy
 mbol: the circle. Each thread added becomes a part of our shared story—a
  living archive of the people\, energy\, and intention inside the space th
 at night. No art experience is needed\; just presence and a willingness to
  contribute to the weave. With love and rhythm\, Devon Luxmore (They/them)
  Marie Joachin (She/Her) Queer Collective TO Co-Founder\, Ritual @enter_th
 e_ritual @queer_collective_to ‍ The Schedule: 6:30 PM - 7:30 PM: Welcome
  &amp\; Sound Healing from Grounded Harmonic 7:45 PM: Open mic poetry &amp
 \; spoken word set to an ambient 100-110 BPM electronic pulse 8:30 PM - La
 te: Dance and connect through a deep-groove journey of organic\, Afro\, tr
 ibal\, and tech house featuring 6 local queer DJs. ‍
LOCATION:TBA\, Address TO BE ANNOUNCED
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/ritual---gemini-pride-edition
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
