BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It Is Not the Homosexual Who Is Perverse\, But the Society in Whic
 h He Lives
DTSTART:20260603T193000
DTEND:20260603T193000
UID:de910eb646452466f1cee00fc808b755@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Director: Rosa von Praunheim Run Time: 67 min. Format: DCP Rel
 ease Year: 1971 Language: German Starring: Bernd Feuerhelm\, Berryt Bohlen
 \, Ernst Kuchling\, Norbert Losch\, Steven Adamczewski Daniel\, a young ma
 n from the provinces come to the city and moves from one gay subculture to
  the next. His adventures begin on the streets of Berlin\, where the shy b
 runette Daniel meets the blonde Clemens\, who invites him home for coffee 
 and offers him a place to stay. Soon Daniel is living with Clemens and bel
 ieves he has found the love of his life. The two try to imitate a bourgeoi
 s marriage and its lifestyle. But after four months of tedium\, Daniel is 
 cruised by a rich older man who entices him to move into his villa\, where
  he encounters a group of older gays\, pretentious in their appreciations 
 of fine art and classical music\, who fawn over him. Doors Open 30 Minutes
  Before Showtime. ‍
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre\, 1006 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/it-is-not-the-homosexual-who-is-perverse-b
 ut-the-society-in-which-he-lives
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
