BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It Takes a Village Walking Tour
DTSTART:20260606T110000
DTEND:20260606T110000
UID:a205837db2103586ceba061612a0c452@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:From the Bathhouse Raids to St. Charles Tavern\, discover the 
 stories of Toronto’s 2SLGBTQ+ community in the Church-Wellesley Village.
  Join us on a guided walk through Church-Wellesley Village to explore the 
 powerful legacy of Toronto’s 2SLGBTQ+ community. From the resilience sho
 wn during the Bathhouse Raids and the AIDS epidemic to the joy and connect
 ion found at spaces like the Buddies in Bad Times Theatre and the St. Char
 les Tavern\, this tour traces the landmarks of both struggle and celebrati
 on. About the Tour Leader Ella Miller (she/her) is a local writer and edit
 or who specializes in reporting on queerness\, disability\, and rural livi
 ng. She has recently graduated from Toronto Metropolitan University with a
  Bachelor’s of Journalism and minor in 2SLGBTQIA+ studies. Ella has prev
 iously worked as a tour guide at the Old Stone Mill National Historic Site
  in Delta\, Ontario and as an archivist at the Brockville Museum. She curr
 ently works with the Toronto Blue Jays delivering tours of Rogers Centre a
 nd on the history of baseball in the city. Ella is passionate about local 
 history and has been involved in archival and education work since she was
  10 years old. When not working or freelancing\, Ella can likely be found 
 at drag shows on Queen West\, visiting artist alleys and fan conventions\,
  or hanging out with her cat\, Javier. Start Point: Barbara Hall Park (519
  Church Street) Our staff and volunteers will be at the tour&#x27\;s start
 ing location 30 minutes prior to each tour. Please arrive at least 10-15 m
 inutes prior to the start of the tour to allow time for check-in. Feel fre
 e to call us at (647) 542-3450 if you are having trouble finding the start
  location. End Point: City Park Co-Operative Apartments (51 Alexander Stre
 et) Length of Tour: Approximately 90 minutes Distance and Terrain: This to
 ur is approximately 2 kilometres in distance and takes place predominantly
  on paved city sidewalks and streets. Ticket Price and Registration: This 
 tour is provided for $8.00/person. The total cost is $10.05 (includes a $2
 .05 transaction fee). Please note that space is limited on our tours. You 
 may not be able to join a tour group if you have not registered ahead of t
 ime. This tour uses individual audio headsets. All registered participants
  will be provided with an individual headset that will allow you to hear t
 he tour guide throughout the tour. ‍
LOCATION:Barbara Hall Park\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/it-takes-a-village-walking-tour-3
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
