BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:&quot\;Roommates&quot\;: a Pride Salon Concert
DTSTART:20260611T193000
DTEND:20260611T193000
UID:ea6f62f02f923e32a3f8212642f775af@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:An evening of music and stories celebrating the fabulous lives
  of LGBTQ+ classical composers! Come join the Toronto Alternative Chamber 
 Orchestra under the baton of Artistic Director Lauren Yeomans as we celebr
 ate PRIDE MONTH with an exploration of LGBTQ+ composers throughout history
  both in and out of the closet! Discover the provocative worlds of these g
 roundbreaking queer artists as our host\, gadabout Carl Jackson\, sends yo
 u on an adventure of subterfuge and mirth! Bring out your flashiest rainbo
 ws\, pencil in that flapper moustache or don your clutchiest pearls for a 
 night you won&#x27\;t want to miss! This fun and informal concert will run
  around 2 hours with two breaks so you can grab a drink and make friends i
 n between sets The programme includes: Francis Poulenc - Mouvements Perpé
 tuels\, FP 14b Benjamin Britten - Sinfonietta\, Op. 1 Marion Bauer - Conce
 rtino for Oboe\, Clarinet and String Quartet\, Op. 32b (conducted by guest
  assistant conductor Missy Thomas) Franz Schubert - Ganymed\, D 544 (with 
 a special appearance by Christopher Dunham\, Baritone) Franz Schubert - Oc
 tet in F major\, D 803 Tickets are $40 for adults and $30 for under 30 and
  artsworkers* available at the door or for purchase in advance here! *NB: 
 Every dollar of ticket sales goes directly towards our operating costs inc
 luding venue and musician fees. That said\, TACO strongly believes that fi
 nances should not be a barrier to accessing the arts. If you would like to
  come to this concert but are unable to pay the full ticket price\, or if 
 you are interested in paying for someone to attend this concert who may ot
 herwise not be able to do so\, please email us at info@torontoalternativec
 hamberorchestra.ca. ‍
LOCATION:Cake Cabaret\, 627 Danforth Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/roommates-a-pride-salon-concert
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea4Tea - An All Trans and Nonbinary Comedy Show!
DTSTART:20260611T200000
DTEND:20260611T200000
UID:f3877f3abd77dfea9f2f4d7c65cb6868@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Pride with a hilarious night of trans and / or nonbi
 nary comedians spilling the tea! Toronto! Come check out this very special
  comedy show featuring EXCLUSIVELY trans and / or nonbinary comedians! Tea
 4Tea is all about having a blast while gathering in community\, celebratin
 g the amazing trans comedic talent right here locally\, and getting some h
 ard earned trans and queer joy! Come and enjoy a fun night of comedy and c
 arry on with your Pride celebrations feeling like your most amazing (sligh
 tly lit!) selves\, or be home in bed by 11 if that&#x27\;s your vibe! Your
  Tea4Tea comedians are: Ajahnis Charley (@ajahnischarley\, they/them\, Thi
 s Hour Has 22 Minutes\, The Beaverton\, Just for Laughs New Faces) Bee Ber
 trand (@beebertrandcomedy\, he/him\, Just for Laughs New Faces\, tour-mate
  with Biff Naked\, Queer Trash Triva\, Bad Gay Advice\, Bee Bertrand and P
 als) Bren D&#x27\;Souza (@brendasouz\, they/them\, Just for Laughs\, Roast
  Battle Canada) Ava Val (@avavalcomedy\, she/her\, John Candy Comedy Award
 \, CBC\, CTV\, OutTV\, Crave\, Just for Laughs\, Halifax &amp\; Winnipeg C
 omedy Festivals\, Canada&#x27\;s Got Talent) Hosted and produced by Anna S
 ebastien (@annasebastiencomedy\, they/them\, Just for Laughs Toronto\, Fre
 sh Hot Babes All Fem &amp\; Queer Comedy). Doors 7 30 pm\, show 8 pm! Tick
 ets are $25 (we love to pay trans &amp\; enby folx fairly for their labour
 !) but all are welcome regardless of means - DM @annasebastiencomedy on In
 stagram for Pay What You Can tickets / community pricing. --- The venue: T
 he show takes place in the front cafe area of the Theatre Centre. The entr
 ance is via the glass doors just off Queen St. W. Seating is self assigned
  and primarily at-grade single occupancy\, unfixed chairs. A few bar seats
  are also available The entrance\, performance area\, and washrooms are al
 l at-grade and accessible for mobility aid users There is a single stall\,
  wheelchair accessible gender neutral washroom available as well as commun
 al gendered &#x27\;men&#x27\; and &#x27\;women&#x27\; washrooms There are 
 non-alcoholic and alcholic beverages available for purchase. There is no k
 itchen / food available at the venue (but lots of great food options nearb
 y). No purchase is required on top of your ticket (but support the venue i
 f you are so inclined!) Community: All are welcome including respectful al
 lies that recognize this is a trans-forward space where we don&#x27\;t ass
 ume anyone&#x27\;s pronouns\, gender\, or orientation\, and where any sort
  of oppressive or creepy behaviour won&#x27\;t fly Performers are encourag
 ed to keep the vibes as comfy and inclusive as possible and agree to commu
 nity guidelines which include no aggressive crowd work\, avoiding topics l
 ikely to be triggering in a trans space\, and no &quot\;punching down&quot
 \; Questions? Nervous about coming out? Just want to say hey before the sh
 ow? Feel free to reach out to the host and producer Anna on IG at @annaseb
 astiencomedy or via email at anna.sebastien.comedy@gmail.com - its all abo
 ut community! We all want a sexy\, healthy Pride month! If you are feeling
  sick\, please stay home! Refund requests will be honoured up to 24 hours 
 before the show Masks are not mandatory but strongly encouraged ‍
LOCATION:The Theatre Centre\, 1115 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/tea4tea---an-all-trans-and-nonbinary-comed
 y-show
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
